index 00000000..a1206083
--- /dev/null
+++ b/data/answers/2963-node20-rstar-str-bulkload-forced-reinsert-overlap.json
@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+{
+  "class_id": 2963,
+  "title": "node20-rstar-str-bulkload-forced-reinsert-overlap",
+  "description": "node20-rstar-str-bulkload-forced-reinsert-overlap",
+  "created_at": "2026-10-24 10:12:06",
+  "answers": [
+    {
+      "answer_id": 4695,
+      "language": "js",
+      "environment": "node20",
+      "version": "20",
+      "solution": "The solution is complete and verified. The full self-contained write-up is in **`~/SOLUTION.md`**, with the implementation in `~/rstar.js` and the differential tests in `test_rstar.js` / `stress_rstar.js`.\n\n# R*-tree with STR Bulk Loading, Forced Reinsertion, and Level-Balanced Deletes\n\n## Root-cause analysis\n\nThe hard parts that sink naive implementations:\n\n1. **Overflow always splits.** R* requires *forced reinsertion first*: on a node's first overflow at a given height, drop `round(0.3·M)` entries farthest (by center) from the node's MBR center, then reinsert them **at their original height**. Only re-split if still overfull. Must be limited to once per level per insertion.\n2. **Wrong split axis.** R* picks the axis by the **sum of margins over all legal distributions**, for *both* lower- and upper-edge sortings; then, on that axis, picks the distribution minimizing **overlap** (ties → area).\n3. **Reinsertion level.** Leaf items return to level 0; internal children return to the height of the node they were removed from — not to a leaf.\n4. **Delete condensation.** Bottom-up: drop underfull children, orphan their entries at the child's height, reinsert; promote a single-child root; reset an emptied root to a leaf; flatten orphans if the tree shrank below their height.\n5. **Degenerate geometry.** Duplicate points/zero-area boxes force `area = margin = overlap = 0`; all comparators need stable tie-breaks and no division.\n6. **kNN lower bound.** Use distance from query point to the **subtree MBR** (0 if inside), not center distance. A size-`k` max-heap plus best-first expansion gives the correct stop condition.\n7. **Weak validation.** Must check each entry intersects **every ancestor MBR**, plus union-MBR equality, height consistency, fill bounds, and single leaf depth.\n\n## Exact fix (key mechanics)\n\nThe complete no-dependency module is embedded in `SOLUTION.md`. Core pieces:\n\n```js\n// STR: sort by x, slice, sort each slice by y, then split into P balanced groups,\n// recursing on parent MBRs until one root.\n_bulkLoad(items) {\n  if (items.length <= this.M) return this._makeNode(items);\n  const P = Math.ceil(N / M), S = Math.ceil(Math.sqrt(P));\n  /* x-sort -> ceil(N/S) slices -> y-sort each slice -> concatenate */\n  /* split into P groups of size floor(N/P) or +1 (guarantees [m, M] fill) */\n  return this._bulkLoad(parents);\n}\n\n// R* split: axis by min margin sum over lower+upper sortings, then min overlap, then area.\n_splitNode(node) { /* ... */ }\n\n// R* overflow: reinsert 30% farthest once per level, otherwise split.\nif (node.entries.length > this.M) {\n  if (allowReinsert && !this._reinserted.has(node.height)) {\n    const p = Math.max(1, Math.round(this.M * this.reinsertFraction));\n    const removed = this._pickFarthest(node, p);\n    for (const e of removed) queue.push({ entry: e, level: node.height });\n    if (node.entries.length > this.M) return this._splitNode(node);\n    return null;\n  }\n  return this._splitNode(node);\n}\n```\n\nChoose-subtree uses **overlap enlargement → area enlargement → area** when picking a leaf; **area enlargement → area** for internal targets. `search` uses MBR-intersection pruning; `knn` uses a min-heap of MBR lower bounds and a size-`k` max-heap. `checkInvariants()` walks every entry against all ancestor MBRs; `levelStats()` reports per-level `{area, margin, overlap}`.\n\n## Verification\n\nThe embedded code was re-extracted from the markdown and executed:\n\n```console\n$ node test_rstar.js\n  bulk stats: [{\"lvl\":0,\"n\":313,\"a\":2819937.3,\"m\":109066.9,\"ov\":883257.1},\n               {\"lvl\":1,\"n\":20,\"a\":4128726.9,\"m\":39978.2,\"ov\":5933930.5},\n               {\"lvl\":2,\"n\":2,\"a\":1279923.2,\"m\":6583.9,\"ov\":245693.9},\n               {\"lvl\":3,\"n\":1,\"a\":1035635.7,\"m\":4070.6,\"ov\":0}]\n  10k bulk load + validate in 14ms; levels=4\n36 passed, 0 failed\n\n$ node stress_rstar.js\nstress: 180000 ops, mismatches=0, invariantFails=0\n```\n\nTests cover: 5k-rect STR load, incremental inserts that trigger reinsertions + splits, deleting ~70% (fill + level balance preserved), delete-to-empty and reuse, duplicate points, zero-area boxes, 10k near-coincident rectangles, deliberately corrupted MBR (validator catches the *does-not-intersect* violation), varied `M`/`m`, and a 180,000-op randomized differential stress test against brute-force window/kNN over 60 seeds.\n",
