+      "solution": "Done. The verified solution is written to **`~/xfs_ag_reconciliation_audit.md`** (1267 lines), with the runnable auditor at **`~/xfs_ag_audit.sh`** and the fixture/test harness at `make_fixture.py` / `test_audit.py`.\n\n## What the solution does\n\n`xfs_ag_audit.sh` is a single self-contained bash+awk program that parses `xxd` / `xxd -g1` / `xxd -p` / `hexdump -C -v` dumps and reconciles one AG's three free-space structures:\n\n- decodes AGF, AGI, AGFL and every CRC `AB3B`/`AB3C` block;\n- walks each btree from the AGF root, checking levels, `numrecs` bounds, sibling back/forward links and full sibling-chain coverage;\n- reconciles `bnobt` vs `cntbt` both as multisets of `(start,count)` and as merged block coverage;\n- validates AGFL slot count/wraparound, duplicates and disjointness from btree extents;\n- verifies `agf_freeblks`, `agf_longest`, `agf_btreeblks` (non-root only) and `agf_flcount`;\n- emits `OFFENDER|<code>|<detail>` lines and exits non-zero.\n\n## Root causes it guards against\n\n1. CRC short btree header is **56 bytes** (`0x38`), not 16.\n2. Internal nodes store **all keys then all pointers** (`maxrecs_node = 336` for 4 K blocks), not interleaved.\n3. **Root `bb_level = agf_level - 1`** (single-leaf tree has `agf_level=1`, `bb_level=0`).\n4. AGFL header is **36 bytes**, slot count derived from sector size, circular `flfirst..fllast` range.\n5. `agf_freeblks` counts **btree extents only**; AGFL blocks are separate and must be disjoint.\n6. `agf_btreeblks` counts **only non-root** blocks.\n7. `cntbt` is ordered by `(count,start)`, so overlap detection must sort by `start` first.\n8. `xxd` ASCII can contain `|`, so the parser keys off the offset delimiter, not `|`.\n\n## Verification\n\n```\n$ ./xfs_ag_audit.sh -q -i agi.hex agf.hex agfl.hex bno_4.hex cnt_5.hex ; echo $?\n0        # healthy single-leaf AG\n\n$ python3 test_audit.py\nPASS healthy  PASS multilevel  PASS agf_magic  PASS freeblks ... PASS dup_rec\nPASS bad_magic PASS numrecs PASS level PASS sib PASS unreached\n18/18 cases passed\n```\n\nThe suite covers all four hexdump dialects, manifest mode, AGFL wraparound, a genuine two-level 505-extent tree with chained leaves, and one mutation per offender class. The markdown includes the full script plus both test files in an appendix so the result is fully reproducible.\n",
