+<p>The randomized cross-check used <code>cryptography</code>'s <code>ChaCha20Poly1305</code> purely as an <strong>external reference oracle</strong> (the solution module imports nothing from it) over 300 random cases spanning key/nonce/AAD/plaintext lengths <code>{0,1,7,12,15,16,17,31,32,33,63,64,100,255,256,1000,4096}</code> and confirmed byte-identical ciphertext and tag, plus AAD-tamper rejection.</p>
+<p>Check that the solution has no forbidden imports:</p>
+<pre><code class="language-bash">grep -nE &quot;cryptography|nacl&quot; chacha20poly1305.py || echo &quot;clean: no cryptography/nacl imports&quot;
+# clean: no cryptography/nacl imports
+</code></pre>
+<h2>Notes on the important properties</h2>
+<ul>
+<li><strong>Detached tag exactness:</strong> <code>aead_encrypt</code> returns <code>(ciphertext, tag)</code> and <code>aead_decrypt</code> takes the tag separately; the tag is computed over <code>aad‖pad16(aad)‖ct‖pad16(ct)‖le64(len_aad)‖le64(len_ct)</code> and nothing else.</li>
+<li><strong>1-byte <code>0x01</code> rule:</strong> implemented exactly in <code>poly1305_mac</code> via <code>int.from_bytes(block + b'\x01', 'little')</code>, so a short final block contributes <code>block_value + 2**(8*len(block))</code>.</li>
+<li><strong>Constant time:</strong> <code>_ct_equal</code> XOR-folds every byte and never returns early within an equal-length comparison; verification happens before decryption, so a bad tag yields no plaintext.</li>
+<li><strong>Partial final block:</strong> <code>chacha20_encrypt</code> processes <code>data[off:off+64]</code>, using only the needed keystream bytes.</li>
+<li><strong>Performance:</strong> ~4 ms for a 4 KiB encrypt+tag on this machine, roughly 50× under the 200 ms budget.</li>
+</ul>
