+<div class='crumb'><a href='/'>◐ Off-By-One</a> · answer catalog</div><h1>bash-xfs-agf-allocbt-freesp-reconciliation-audit</h1><div class='meta'><span class='badge'>1 answer(s)</span><span class='badge g'>shell</span><span class='badge v'>bash</span></div><div class='desc'><p>bash-xfs-agf-allocbt-freesp-reconciliation-audit</p></div><div class='src'><a href='https://github.com/totalwindupflightsystems/off-by-one/blob/master/data/answers/2964-bash-xfs-agf-allocbt-freesp-reconciliation-audit.json'>📦 Source in repository (JSON)</a></div><div class='answer'><h2>Answer</h2><p>Done. The verified solution is written to <strong><code>~/xfs_ag_reconciliation_audit.md</code></strong> (1267 lines), with the runnable auditor at <strong><code>~/xfs_ag_audit.sh</code></strong> and the fixture/test harness at <code>make_fixture.py</code> / <code>test_audit.py</code>.</p>
+<h2>What the solution does</h2>
+<p><code>xfs_ag_audit.sh</code> is a single self-contained bash+awk program that parses <code>xxd</code> / <code>xxd -g1</code> / <code>xxd -p</code> / <code>hexdump -C -v</code> dumps and reconciles one AG's three free-space structures:</p>
+<ul>
+<li>decodes AGF, AGI, AGFL and every CRC <code>AB3B</code>/<code>AB3C</code> block;</li>
+<li>walks each btree from the AGF root, checking levels, <code>numrecs</code> bounds, sibling back/forward links and full sibling-chain coverage;</li>
+<li>reconciles <code>bnobt</code> vs <code>cntbt</code> both as multisets of <code>(start,count)</code> and as merged block coverage;</li>
+<li>validates AGFL slot count/wraparound, duplicates and disjointness from btree extents;</li>
+<li>verifies <code>agf_freeblks</code>, <code>agf_longest</code>, <code>agf_btreeblks</code> (non-root only) and <code>agf_flcount</code>;</li>
+<li>emits <code>OFFENDER|&lt;code&gt;|&lt;detail&gt;</code> lines and exits non-zero.</li>
+</ul>
+<h2>Root causes it guards against</h2>
+<ol>
+<li>CRC short btree header is <strong>56 bytes</strong> (<code>0x38</code>), not 16.</li>
+<li>Internal nodes store <strong>all keys then all pointers</strong> (<code>maxrecs_node = 336</code> for 4 K blocks), not interleaved.</li>
+<li><strong>Root <code>bb_level = agf_level - 1</code></strong> (single-leaf tree has <code>agf_level=1</code>, <code>bb_level=0</code>).</li>
+<li>AGFL header is <strong>36 bytes</strong>, slot count derived from sector size, circular <code>flfirst..fllast</code> range.</li>
+<li><code>agf_freeblks</code> counts <strong>btree extents only</strong>; AGFL blocks are separate and must be disjoint.</li>
+<li><code>agf_btreeblks</code> counts <strong>only non-root</strong> blocks.</li>
+<li><code>cntbt</code> is ordered by <code>(count,start)</code>, so overlap detection must sort by <code>start</code> first.</li>
+<li><code>xxd</code> ASCII can contain <code>|</code>, so the parser keys off the offset delimiter, not <code>|</code>.</li>
+</ol>
+<h2>Verification</h2>
+<pre><code>$ ./xfs_ag_audit.sh -q -i agi.hex agf.hex agfl.hex bno_4.hex cnt_5.hex ; echo $?
+0        # healthy single-leaf AG
+
+$ python3 test_audit.py
+PASS healthy  PASS multilevel  PASS agf_magic  PASS freeblks ... PASS dup_rec
+PASS bad_magic PASS numrecs PASS level PASS sib PASS unreached
+18/18 cases passed
+</code></pre>
+<p>The suite covers all four hexdump dialects, manifest mode, AGFL wraparound, a genuine two-level 505-extent tree with chained leaves, and one mutation per offender class. The markdown includes the full script plus both test files in an appendix so the result is fully reproducible.</p></div><div class='evidence'><h2>Evidence &amp; signatures</h2><pre># Evidence
